# sqlfluff cannot parse a dbt snapshot block.
#
# `{% snapshot %}` is a dbt tag, not Jinja, so the jinja templater fails the
# whole file with "Encountered unknown tag 'snapshot'". Only `templater = dbt`
# understands it, and the root .sqlfluff explains at length why this project
# does not switch to it (it would need dbt installed in the pre-commit venv and
# a reachable warehouse, turning a lint finding into a hard error on every
# machine with no stack running).
#
# So the two snapshot definitions are excluded from linting. They are ten lines
# of SELECT each wrapped in a config block, they are covered by `dbt build`
# like every other node, and their output is asserted by the SCD2 tests in
# models/marts/_marts.yml. Excluding them costs nothing that is not checked
# somewhere stricter.
#
# Nothing else is excluded. Every model, test and macro in this project is
# linted.
snapshots/

# dbt's own output. target/ holds COMPILED sql - dbt's rendering of these
# models plus every generic test it generated - and logs/ holds dbt.log. Both
# are regenerated by the next build and neither is tracked, so linting them
# reports on machine-written text nobody can fix.
#
# The pre-commit hook never saw them (it only lints STAGED files and both are
# gitignored). This line makes a local `sqlfluff lint analytics/dbt` agree with
# what the hook actually checks, so "clean locally" and "clean in CI" mean the
# same thing.
target/
logs/
